WEBVTT

00:01:52.560 --> 00:01:58.160
Clone...

00:02:23.790 --> 00:02:24.780
What is it?

00:02:27.190 --> 00:02:28.220
Nothing special.

00:02:45.210 --> 00:02:46.200
What is it?

00:02:47.250 --> 00:02:48.580
Nothing special.

00:03:07.300 --> 00:03:08.820
What's the matter?

00:03:09.630 --> 00:03:12.330
I'm exhausted somehow.

00:03:13.000 --> 00:03:15.030
Yeah, me too.

00:03:16.110 --> 00:03:18.980
Hey, give me a little?

00:03:18.980 --> 00:03:20.010
Huh?

00:03:20.010 --> 00:03:21.500
Just a little!

00:03:30.360 --> 00:03:31.720
I feel like I'll get a nosebleed.

00:03:50.240 --> 00:03:51.770
Just a little...

00:03:52.410 --> 00:03:53.310
Okay?

00:04:28.750 --> 00:04:29.680
Oh!

00:04:37.990 --> 00:04:39.120
What...

00:04:40.190 --> 00:04:42.990
It's okay. It'll wear off soon.

00:04:45.030 --> 00:04:48.800
Come to think of it, I was told not to do this kind of thing too much.

00:04:49.800 --> 00:04:50.860
By who?

00:04:51.770 --> 00:04:53.100
Fujisaki...

00:04:54.570 --> 00:04:58.570
You know, isn't it about time you had a mind of your own?

00:04:59.580 --> 00:05:01.670
Instead of just going along with whatever anyone tells you.

00:05:02.650 --> 00:05:05.280
But Fujisaki is...

00:05:05.280 --> 00:05:11.960
That guy has no emotions, but we're different.

00:05:11.960 --> 00:05:13.980
We get hurt, we get worried...

00:05:15.960 --> 00:05:19.260
At those kinds of times, what's wrong with using Dynamis?

00:06:47.990 --> 00:06:50.180
So we owe you another one, eh?

00:06:50.860 --> 00:06:53.550
The girl you brought back this time is a little different.

00:06:53.960 --> 00:06:57.830
If you meddle with her the wrong way, you'll end up like your chief.

00:06:59.000 --> 00:07:01.400
So what is it you want to talk about?

00:07:01.400 --> 00:07:04.100
You received quite a sum as a contract fee, right?

00:07:04.100 --> 00:07:05.400
From the Countess?

00:07:06.540 --> 00:07:08.200
So what about it?

00:07:08.740 --> 00:07:12.110
Once again, without me you wouldn't have been able to catch her.

00:07:12.840 --> 00:07:17.220
So I was thinking of claiming a suitable reward.

00:07:17.220 --> 00:07:19.920
You bastard, you think you're gonna extort money from a yakuza?

00:07:19.920 --> 00:07:24.620
A yakuza? Why, I thought you were an upstanding broker.

00:07:26.890 --> 00:07:29.720
There's something on which I'd like your cooperation.

00:07:30.800 --> 00:07:32.190
It's a simple request.

00:07:36.100 --> 00:07:37.470
Guess I've got no choice.

00:07:55.050 --> 00:07:57.780
It seems to me this is the second time we've met here too.

00:07:58.390 --> 00:08:00.580
Isn't it about time you gave it up?

00:08:03.660 --> 00:08:06.690
Is your being a bad loser also inherited from your mother?

00:08:08.770 --> 00:08:14.640
My mother certainly was the lowest of the low, but you're below that.

00:08:14.640 --> 00:08:15.700
You're a beast.

00:08:19.880 --> 00:08:23.040
The one who had relations with a beast was you, wasn't it?

00:08:34.530 --> 00:08:37.460
As we're both beasts here, let's get along with each other.

00:08:39.230 --> 00:08:41.530
You were at Heaven's Gate, right?

00:08:45.000 --> 00:08:50.300
I just now remembered something from the day my mother and I returned to Japan.

00:09:01.090 --> 00:09:02.950
You came to where we were, didn't you?

00:09:08.590 --> 00:09:11.030
Your eyes at that time...

00:09:11.030 --> 00:09:13.050
I can't describe the look in your eyes.

00:09:16.230 --> 00:09:19.470
But you looked so happy when you were a girl.

00:09:25.040 --> 00:09:27.550
I wonder what it was that changed you?

00:09:27.550 --> 00:09:29.050
Jealousy?

00:09:29.050 --> 00:09:30.380
Rage?

00:09:30.380 --> 00:09:32.220
Hatred?

00:09:32.220 --> 00:09:32.980
Resentment?

00:09:35.890 --> 00:09:37.320
Probably all of those.

00:09:42.360 --> 00:09:43.730
Running away would be futile.

00:09:44.360 --> 00:09:46.300
I'll go anywhere.

00:09:48.170 --> 00:09:49.860
I can go anyplace,

00:09:50.940 --> 00:09:52.460
...because I have this child,

00:09:53.740 --> 00:09:55.500
...so I can even use Dynamis.

00:10:10.050 --> 00:10:14.450
Kiyoko?

00:10:15.290 --> 00:10:20.890
Kiyoko!

00:10:27.510 --> 00:10:29.600
<i>Kiyoko! Kiyoko!</i>

00:10:29.810 --> 00:10:33.680
<i>Please wait, Master Tatsuya. Miss Kiyoko is fine.</i>

00:10:36.380 --> 00:10:37.370
<i>Come in.</i>

00:10:41.120 --> 00:10:43.290
<i>Her cardiac function is declining.</i>

00:10:43.290 --> 00:10:46.520
<i>Her pulse is weak, systolic blood pressure is 50.</i>

00:10:47.090 --> 00:10:48.420
<i>We can't get a reading for diastolic.</i>

00:10:50.900 --> 00:10:52.590
<i>She's in very critical condition.</i>

00:10:53.800 --> 00:10:55.160
<i>And the baby in her womb?</i>

00:10:56.200 --> 00:10:58.300
<i>The fetus is fine.</i>

00:10:58.300 --> 00:10:59.670
<i>However, we can no longer...</i>

00:11:11.880 --> 00:11:12.980
<i>Kiyoko!</i>

00:11:13.480 --> 00:11:14.950
<i>It's me, Kiyoko!</i>

00:11:15.950 --> 00:11:16.920
<i>Kiyoko!</i>

00:11:26.900 --> 00:11:28.090
Tatsuya?

00:11:36.210 --> 00:11:37.200
A dream?

00:11:59.030 --> 00:12:00.360
What's wrong?

00:12:01.630 --> 00:12:04.470
I just now heard a crash from someone...

00:12:04.470 --> 00:12:05.960
A crash?

00:12:09.210 --> 00:12:11.870
Are you sure it wasn't a strange dream?

00:12:15.910 --> 00:12:17.880
Could you let us out now?

00:12:17.880 --> 00:12:19.180
Excuse me, driver!

00:12:35.330 --> 00:12:36.360
A dream?

00:12:49.850 --> 00:12:50.970
Is this a dream too?

00:13:14.840 --> 00:13:18.140
It's somehow as if we're in a bad dream that goes on and on.

00:13:18.780 --> 00:13:23.180
When we wake up there will be a real world, and the real us.

00:13:24.220 --> 00:13:25.770
Let's go to the real world.

00:13:32.160 --> 00:13:34.180
I know your hands right away, Tatsuya.

00:13:35.130 --> 00:13:40.150
Warm, a little damp, gentle hands, like a girl's.

00:13:46.900 --> 00:13:48.060
Daddy!

00:14:26.310 --> 00:14:27.400
Kiyoko...

00:14:28.410 --> 00:14:29.540
Huh?

00:14:45.360 --> 00:14:46.760
Well, shall we go?

00:14:48.530 --> 00:14:49.460
Huh?

00:14:55.370 --> 00:15:00.280
Daddy says he still has work to do. Let's go home ahead of him.

00:15:00.880 --> 00:15:02.140
Home?

00:15:02.750 --> 00:15:03.810
That's right.

00:15:05.250 --> 00:15:06.840
Let's go home.

00:15:07.490 --> 00:15:08.470
Okay...

00:15:11.860 --> 00:15:13.050
Mommy...

00:15:13.620 --> 00:15:14.960
What is it?

00:15:15.260 --> 00:15:16.560
Nothing.

00:16:00.370 --> 00:16:01.930
Where am I?

00:16:05.480 --> 00:16:07.570
Have I died?

00:16:24.830 --> 00:16:26.060
Who are you?

00:16:27.330 --> 00:16:30.200
I've been waiting all this time for you to come.

00:16:30.840 --> 00:16:32.200
Tens of millions of years...

00:16:34.170 --> 00:16:35.660
Billions of years...

00:16:37.370 --> 00:16:39.640
Hey, let's play together.

00:16:42.210 --> 00:16:43.480
What's that?

00:16:46.250 --> 00:16:47.340
A tuning fork.

00:16:48.250 --> 00:16:50.740
You use it when you tune a piano.

00:17:29.660 --> 00:17:30.820
<i>Kiyoko!</i>

00:17:31.530 --> 00:17:33.760
<i>Kiyoko, it's me! Do you recognize me?</i>

00:17:38.240 --> 00:17:40.070
I'm right here.

00:17:42.670 --> 00:17:43.800
Tatsuya?

00:17:45.010 --> 00:17:47.710
Here, take this. It's your tuning fork, Kiyoko.

00:17:49.480 --> 00:17:50.750
Tuning fork?

00:17:50.750 --> 00:17:53.180
I was ringing it this whole time.

00:17:54.120 --> 00:17:56.210
I thought you might be able to hear it.

00:17:57.560 --> 00:18:00.390
I could hear it. Thanks.

00:18:04.660 --> 00:18:07.430
Don't go off anywhere again, okay?

00:18:08.100 --> 00:18:11.000
Promise me you won't go anywhere alone.

00:18:13.200 --> 00:18:14.210
Okay...

00:18:14.210 --> 00:18:15.570
That's for keeps.

00:18:18.340 --> 00:18:22.710
In a dream, I met Dad and Mom.

00:18:24.080 --> 00:18:25.280
You did?

00:18:25.920 --> 00:18:30.980
Dad was laughing kindly, and Mom looked attractive.

00:18:31.660 --> 00:18:32.640
Really?

00:18:33.990 --> 00:18:40.330
I'm sorry, your big sister has all the good memories to herself.

00:18:41.170 --> 00:18:44.260
It's ridiculous to say sorry, Kiyoko,

00:18:45.040 --> 00:18:49.970
...since I have lots of fun memories of playing with you.

00:18:51.240 --> 00:18:52.470
Tatsuya...

00:18:53.040 --> 00:18:55.710
I have lots, and lots!

00:18:57.280 --> 00:19:01.910
I wanted to make a lot more memories with you, Tatsuya.

00:19:03.150 --> 00:19:06.250
That's right, you have to hurry up and get well.

00:19:06.960 --> 00:19:09.930
A lot of fun things are waiting for you in the future.

00:19:12.100 --> 00:19:14.790
I'll be a papa to the baby.

00:19:16.930 --> 00:19:23.430
I'm sure you'll make a good mother, Kiyoko. After all, you raised me.

00:19:25.740 --> 00:19:28.300
Tatsuya, I'm sorry.

00:19:29.610 --> 00:19:33.410
Kiyoko, you're going to circle the globe tuning pianos, right?

00:19:34.490 --> 00:19:38.980
You'll need help, so I'll come along with you and hold the baby.

00:19:40.860 --> 00:19:42.530
I'm sorry...

00:19:42.530 --> 00:19:45.790
In place of lullabies, let's let it listen to the piano.

00:19:47.000 --> 00:19:49.120
We'll bring it up to have a good ear for music.

00:19:50.000 --> 00:19:51.630
Like you, Kiyoko.

00:19:53.570 --> 00:19:54.540
Kiyoko!

00:19:56.510 --> 00:19:57.770
I'm cold...

00:19:59.980 --> 00:20:01.340
I feel like I'm going to freeze.

00:20:09.320 --> 00:20:12.120
How's that? Are you warm now?

00:20:14.490 --> 00:20:15.890
I'm warm.

00:20:23.130 --> 00:20:26.830
I like your body; it's so warm.

00:20:28.010 --> 00:20:32.310
I love you too, Kiyoko.

00:20:45.990 --> 00:20:46.960
Fu!

00:20:54.300 --> 00:20:55.530
Sorry...

00:20:57.330 --> 00:21:00.270
I told you to go easy on that, didn't I?

00:21:00.740 --> 00:21:04.000
Yeah, but it's been nothing but unbearable stuff!

00:21:04.510 --> 00:21:08.410
Both the stuff about us, and this stuff with Kiyoko.

00:21:26.160 --> 00:21:30.000
She told me she was warm, but...

00:21:31.000 --> 00:21:32.900
She said so, but...

00:21:34.840 --> 00:21:37.640
Kiyoko's gotten cold,

00:21:38.440 --> 00:21:41.170
...and she won't wake up for me any more.

00:23:24.620 --> 00:23:26.850
There was a war at the beginning of this century.

00:23:26.980 --> 00:23:29.420
Even the cradle of civilization is in this state.

00:23:29.420 --> 00:23:31.110
Mesopotamian civilization...

00:23:31.260 --> 00:23:33.320
Uruk is also the homeland of the world's oldest story,

00:23:33.320 --> 00:23:35.230
..."The Epic of Gilgamesh."

00:23:35.230 --> 00:23:37.160
Gilgamesh is the name of a legendary king,

00:23:37.160 --> 00:23:39.830
...who was said to be part god and part human.

00:23:39.830 --> 00:23:43.820
Gilgamesh, a tyrant whom the legend depicts as courageous and fierce.

00:23:43.900 --> 00:23:46.140
The people were made to suffer under his tyranny.

00:23:46.140 --> 00:23:49.440
But before him appeared a man named Enkidu.

00:23:49.440 --> 00:23:50.670
At first the two were foes...

00:23:50.670 --> 00:23:53.670
Shut up, shut up! Shut your mouth, you old hag!
